    "body": "Current Chromium behavior gives us two useful anchors for specifying this.\n\nWhen a serial port opens, Blink registers `kWebSerial` with `DisableAggressiveThrottling()`. When its execution context is destroyed, `SerialPort::ContextDestroyed()` immediately resets the Mojo port connection.\n\nWhat remains unclear is the middle state: a page that is frozen but not destroyed.\n\nDefining that transition explicitly would help both BFCache behavior and latency/resource predictability: whether the port closes, I/O pauses, pending operations reject, and how connect/disconnect events are reconciled after resume.\n",
